course: dictionary
lesson: 484
title: Who is an artist?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An artist is a person who makes art, such as paintings, drawings or sculptures. «The Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama makes Infinity Mirror Rooms» tells you an artist can also create rooms full of mirrors and light.
explain: Artist can also mean a performer, like a singer, musician, actor or dancer, as in «a recording artist». It can also mean anyone who does something with great skill, as in «a real artist with a football». Look at the clues around the word to see which meaning fits.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «Big games are made by teams: programmers, artists, designers, writers», the list shows that artists are the people who make how a game looks and feels, so here an artist is a maker.
fact: An artist is a person who paints, draws, makes sculptures or other works of art.
fact: An artist can also be a performer, such as a singer, musician, actor or dancer.
fact: «A real artist with a football» means someone who does something with great skill.
fact: Phrases with artist include «street artist», «make-up artist» and «artist's palette».
fact: An installation is art that fills a room, like Yayoi Kusama's Infinity Mirror Rooms.
exercise: «The Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama makes Infinity Mirror Rooms.» What is an artist in this sentence? | A room full of mirrors | *A person who makes art | A football team | A type of light
exercise: «Big games are made by teams: programmers, artists, designers, writers.» In this list, what do the artists do? | *Make the look and feel of the game | Sell the game in shops | Test the game for bugs | Play the game all night
exercise: Ana says «a real artist with a football» means a painter who uses paint on a ball. What does artist mean here? | A person who paints pictures | A ball covered in paint | *Someone who does something with great skill | A football coach
test: «A recording artist» is a singer or musician who makes records. What kind of artist is this? | A sculptor | A painter | A museum guard | *A performer
test: In «the artist's palette», what is a palette? | A tray for mixing paint | *A kind of football | A stage light | A pair of shoes
exam: Which meaning of artist fits «Going to shows or buying music straight from the artist helps them far more»? | A machine that makes music | A painter in a gallery | *A musician who performs | A critic who writes reviews
